# Benchmark scenario: Skyrim new-game intro (cart ride).
#
# The script syncs to the stable main menu (any draw count >= 9 held for 2 s),
# starts a new game, syncs to the "Start a new game?" confirmation, confirms it,
# then lets the intro cinematic play.  The runner measures a fixed 30 s window
# (script frames 2400..4200 relative to the second sync) inside the cart ride,
# dumps three frames after the window for visual comparisons and quits cleanly.
#
# Frame numbers after a waitsteady are counted from the moment it is satisfied.
0 waitsteady 120 9
10 tap 28                # DIK_RETURN: NEW -> "Start a new game?"
20 waitsteady 90 20      # confirmation dialog is a steady 40-draw screen
80 tap 28                # DIK_RETURN: Yes
4300 dump
4400 dump
4500 dump
4800 quit
